    where: 'Cash flow statement, first adjustment in operating activities. Most companies, including Amazon, embed it inside cost of revenue and operating expenses on the income statement.',
    hist: 'From the cash flow statement. If the company also amortises other items in the same line (for example capitalised content), the line may be wider than PP&E depreciation.',
    fc: 'Depreciation from the PP&E schedule (% of revenue, % of opening net PP&E, or a vintage schedule), plus amortisation of intangibles as a % of the opening intangible balance.',
    fx: 'Income statement: subtracted once to get EBIT (either inside costs or as a separate line, never both). Balance sheet: reduces net PP&E and intangibles. Cash flow: added back in operating activities.',
